course: dictionary
lesson: 5116
title: Intonation: how your voice changes meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intonation is the rise and fall of your voice as you speak. The same words can mean different things depending on whether your voice goes up or down. «You're coming tomorrow?» With a rising voice at the end, it is a question. Said with a falling voice, it is a statement.
explain: Look for clues around the word. The example sentence tells you that raising your voice at the end can turn a statement into a question. When you read a question mark, imagine your voice going up at the end. Then check: does this sound like someone asking?
explain: Music uses the word too. In music, intonation means singing or playing exactly in tune. A singer with good intonation hits each note in the right place.
fact: Intonation is the rise and fall of your voice when you speak.
fact: A rising voice at the end of a sentence often means a question, as in «You're coming tomorrow?»
fact: A falling voice at the end usually sounds like a statement or a full stop.
fact: In music, intonation means singing or playing exactly in tune.
fact: Phrases you may meet are rising intonation, falling intonation and good intonation.
exercise: Which kind of intonation makes «You're coming tomorrow?» sound like a question? | Falling, the voice goes down at the end | *Rising, the voice goes up at the end | Loud, shouting every word | Flat, with no change at all
exercise: In music, what does intonation mean? | Singing very loudly | Playing a song with no notes | *Singing or playing exactly in tune | Writing the lyrics down
exercise: Which phrase describes a voice that goes down at the end of a sentence? | Silent intonation | *Falling intonation | Loud intonation | Rising intonation
test: What does intonation mean when we speak? | The size of the letters you write | The number of words in a sentence | The speed of your words | *The rise and fall of your voice
test: Sam says «Dinner's ready» with a falling voice. What is he most likely doing? | Shouting a warning | *Making a statement | Asking a question | Singing a song
exam: Which sentence is most likely said with rising intonation? | «We went home.» | «I am ready.» | *«Are you ready?» | «Ready.»
